y categories array and total \"0.00\".\n\nWrite JSON to stdout. \"Emit exactly {...}\" \u2014 probably json.dumps output. Let me just print json.dumps(result).\n\nLet me write:\n\n```python\nimport sys, csv, json\nfrom decimal import Decimal, ROUND_HALF_UP\n\ndef main():\n    path = sys.argv[1]\n    with open(path, encoding=\"utf-8\", newline=\"\") as f:\n        reader = csv.DictReader(f)\n        rows = list(reader)\n    amounts = {}\n    total = Decimal(\"0.00\")\n    for row in rows:\n        status = (row.get(\"status\") or \"\").strip().casefold()\n        if status != \"paid\":\n            continue\n        category = (row.get(\"category\") or \"\").strip()\n        if category == \"\":\n            category = \"uncategorized\"\n        category = \" \".join(category.split()).casefold()\n        amount = Decimal(row.get(\"amount\") or \"0\")\n        rounded = amount.quantize(Decimal(\"0.01\"), rounding=ROUND_HALF_UP)\n        amounts[category] = amounts.get(category, Decimal(\"0\")) + rounded\n        total += rounded\n    categories = [\n        {\"category\": name, \"total\": f\"{amount:.2f}\"}\n        for name, amount in sorted(amounts.items())\n    ]\n    result = {\n        \"categories\": categories,\n        \"total\": f\"{total:.2f}\",\n    }\n    print(json.dumps(result))\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n```\n\nWait, \"collapse whitespace\" \u2014 should I collapse before or after casefold? Collapse whitespace and casefold. Blank category -> uncategorized. Blank after collapsing means empty string, so uncategorized.\n\nf\"{amount:.2f}\" for Decimal works? Yes, format spec works with Decimal. f\"{Decimal('10.99'):.2f}\" -> '10.99'. Good.\n\nSum: sum of rounded row amounts; total formatted two decimals.\n\nSort by normalized name.\n\nKeep included categories even when sum is zero \u2014 since we add to amounts dict even with zero amounts, fine.\n\nHeader-only file: DictReader with just header -> rows empty -> categories [], total \"0.00\". Good.\n\nShould JSON be exactly that key order? json.dumps preserves insertion order. Fine.\n\nShould output be a JSON value \u2014 print(json.dumps(result)) produces one JSON value. Good.\n\nEdge: category normalization - \"Books\" vs \"BOOKS\" -> \"books\" both. Collapse whitespace: \"Books  x\" -> \"books x\"? split/join collapses. Casefold.\n\nLet me also handle rows possibly missing keys. Fine.\n\nWrite script, run.",
